  "root_cause_diagnosis": {
    "issue": "Asyncio loopback IPC socket.accept() blocked inside Windows sandbox",
    "mechanism": "Starlette TestClient and anyio initialize an internal event loop using socketpair IPC. On Windows, Python's proactor event loop creates an internal loopback socket pair via _fallback_socketpair calling localhost. Under standard sandbox mode (BypassSandbox: false), local socket binding/connection is blocked, causing socket.accept() to hang indefinitely.",
    "resolution": "Executed pytest with loopback permission enabled (BypassSandbox: true) as per execution rules for local socket test servers. Tests completed in 7.37s with 19/19 passing."
  },
